<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Quiriguá</h1><p class="st-meta">426 CE – 810 CE (approx.) · capital Quiriguá</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Maya kingdom in the Motagua valley that won independence from Copán in 738 and raised the tallest carved stone monuments of the Maya world.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Quiriguá was founded or refounded in 426 CE as a dependency of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/copan">Copán</a>, about 50 kilometres to the south, by agents of Copán's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-yax-kuk-mo">K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo'</a>. It controlled the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/motagua-river">Motagua</a> river, a route for jade and obsidian toward the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kak-tiliw-chan-yopaat">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat</a> was installed under Copán's authority in 724. In 738, probably backed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaan">Kingdom of Kaan</a>, he captured and beheaded Copán's king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waxaklajuun-ubaah-kawiil">Waxaklajuun Ub'aah K'awiil</a>, freeing Quiriguá. He celebrated with enormous sandstone stelae, including Stela E, over 10 metres tall, and zoomorphic boulders carved with long texts.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Quiriguá prospered for several decades after its victory but its last monuments date to about 810, after which it declined. It was declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 1981.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/quirigua.jpg" alt="Quiriguá" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Jan Pešula · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GT_Quirigua_StelaE.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>426 CE – 810 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Quiriguá</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat, Sky Xul</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Guatemala</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Quirigua</dd></dl></aside></div>

